> [!WARNING]
> **A repeated saved finding accounts for two child warnings**
>
> <sub>F5 · Warning · correctness</sub>

`filed` here is `[...ledger.findings(), ...normalized.report.findings]` (`tools.ts:469`), and those two lists overlap whenever the model both saves a finding with `record_finding` and repeats it in `submit_review` — the reason `mergeSavedFindings` dedupes the same pair before posting (`packages/backend/src/services/pr-review/findings.ts:144`). Each copy claims a child warning of its own, so with two children anchored within 5 lines the second warning is matched by a duplicate of an unrelated finding and is never filed or refused. Dedupe the filed findings by path, line, severity and title before pairing them.

```suggestion
	// One filed finding or dismissal accounts for one child warning, so two nearby ones need two. A
	// note does not: downgrading a child's warning is a dismissal, said with its reason. The same
	// finding saved with `record_finding` and repeated in `submit_review` still accounts for one.
	const claimed = new Set<PrReviewFinding | PrReviewChildDismissal>()
	const filedOnce = filed.filter(
		(finding, index) =>
			finding.severity !== "info" &&
			filed.findIndex(
				(other) =>
					other.path === finding.path &&
					other.line === finding.line &&
					other.severity === finding.severity &&
					other.title === finding.title,
			) === index,
	)
	const accounts = [...filedOnce, ...dismissed]
```
